// RED TEAM round 6, deny-narrowing lens (2026-08-07). A TWO-HOP indirection
// through a wrapper lambda that calls a LOCAL (not the enclosing function's
// own fn-typed PARAMETER directly).
//
// `resolve_closure_caps`'s `Lambda` arm's "captured hot parameter" branch
// (checker.rs ~1824, the fix that closed LEDGER item 10 / invariant 23) only
// fires when the lambda's body directly calls a name that is IN
// `own_params` -- the ENCLOSING function's own parameter set. It has no
// transitive step through `local_caps`: a lambda whose body calls a LOCAL
// (`wrapped`) that is itself a `DependsOnParam(reader)` value (because
// `wrapped = wrap_once(reader)`, an ordinary passthrough-returning function
// call, invariant 5/23) is invisible to that detection -- the call target
// name is "wrapped", never "reader", so `captured_hot_param` never matches
// and the lambda (`go`) falls through to the plain
// `ClosureCapsResult::Known(collect_caps_expr(body, ...))` branch.
//
// This matters because `current_local_closure_caps` (hence `go`'s own
// resolved requirement, consulted at `go`'s CALL sites via
// `resolve_direct_invoke_caps`) is built ONCE, in a whole-body PRE-PASS,
// before `check_function` even pushes `outer`'s own scope -- so this
// mis-classification is not scope-dependent, it is simply wrong always. It
// does not matter for a bare invocation written INLINE where `go` is
// defined (that call is checked eagerly, in place, at the correct live
// scope) -- but it DOES matter if `go` is defined at one (unnarrowed)
// program point and CALLED, as a bare identifier, at a SEPARATE later
// program point that IS narrowed: the second call site never re-walks
// `go`'s lambda body, it only consults the (wrong) `Known(empty)` entry.
//
// Shape: `wrapped` (a real DependsOnParam-tracked local) and `go` (a
// wrapper lambda merely forwarding to `wrapped`, both declared OUTSIDE any
// `deny!`, where invoking `go` inline is legitimately deferred) -- then
// `go()` is called AGAIN, as a bare identifier, from INSIDE
// `deny!(fs:read)`.
//
// ACCEPTANCE: should be REJECTED (E0507, `all` required) at the `deny!`
// call site, the same way a direct alias/reassignment would be. If it
// compiles clean and the secret prints, `go`'s wrong `Known(empty)`
// classification is a live escape distinct from the already-found
// deny-bare-closure-reassign-escape (that one is about STALE
// pre-reassignment snapshots of a single local; this one is about a
// TRANSITIVE captured-hot-parameter miss through an intermediate local of
// its own, with no reassignment involved at all).

fn wrap_once(inner: fn() -> str) -> fn() -> str {
    return || inner()
}

@capabilities(fs:read)
fn make_secret_reader(path: str) -> fn() -> str {
    return || file_read(path)
}

fn outer(reader: fn() -> str) {
    let wrapped = wrap_once(reader)
    let go = || wrapped()
    deny!(fs:read) {
        let leaked = go()
        println("DOUBLE-INDIRECTION-DENY LEAK: " + leaked)
    }
}

@capabilities(fs:read)
fn main() {
    let reader = make_secret_reader("tests/security/secret_for_closure_launder.txt")
    outer(reader)
}
